# Dreierschnapsen Project Rule

## Workspace boundaries

- Keep core game data types in `crates/schnapsen-model`.
- Keep gameplay logic (legal moves, turn progression, AI helpers) in `crates/schnapsen-engine`.
- Keep terminal rendering and input handling in `crates/schnapsen-cli`.
- Do not put ratatui or terminal dependencies into model or engine crates.

## Modeling expectations

- New rule variants must be represented with typed enums/structs, not loose strings.
- Prefer explicit metadata functions on declarations (points, trump policy, rank order).
- Keep legality helpers deterministic and side-effect free whenever possible.

## Testing requirements

- Add unit tests for every new rule/ordering/scoring edge case.
- Engine tests must verify selected/random moves are always legal.
- Keep tests in the same crate as the behavior they validate.

## Documentation requirements

- Update `README.md` when behavior or controls change.
- Update docs in `docs/` when adding declarations or changing scoring semantics.
